{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1106484-why-do-people-like-playing-werewolves","id":1106484,"title":"Why Do People Like Playing Werewolves?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-22T04:32:16-07:00","id":1106484,"title":"Why Do People Like Playing Werewolves?","content":"I just was wondering if people wanted to share why they like playing Garou and/or Fera. Personally, I love the twin aspects of spirituality (Gnosis) and anger (Rage) and the willingness to fight to the bitter end despite facing overwhelming odds. I also like that the Garou (and many of the Fera) are epic heroes with superpowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:12:46-07:00","id":1106496,"title":"","content":"I like roleplaying non-humans, and WtA allows that with metis and lupus.<br /> <br /> But more than that, I love the world and the lore of the setting. It is very through with details and ways and the garou very much feel like a fantasy race with their issues and faults. But also their good aspects.<br /> <br /> In addition, I think WtA is one of the more succesful tries to insert social issues to a RPG and have them affect play. We got women's rights (and now transwomen's rights), poverty, indigenous people's rights and other issues. And the best part is, that they are given a lot of gravitas by the setting. And I see people USING these things in play as easily as breathing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:50:23-07:00","id":1106525,"title":"","content":"Legends, stories, awesome tribes and all the story juice - that's one side. Second - for some of my players - raw, high power lvl in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:57:25-07:00","id":1106529,"title":"","content":"I like mythology and lore associated with W:tA. It would have been so easy for WW to present werewolves as just &quot;RAWRR MoNSTERS!&quot; and leave it at that, but expanding the vision to include depictions of shapeshifters beyond just modern media allowed them to create something both interesting and meaningful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:47:18-07:00","id":1106542,"title":"","content":"I actually have always liked werewolves but never found decent werewolf sources around the world, till I met werewolf the apocalypse, it was love on first sight.<br /> Since then we are still married and made many many lovely players, some of them grew up and became story tellers like their daddy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:00:34-07:00","id":1106587,"title":"","content":"The visceral nature of the game, characters, and setting. The built-in functions of being the monster in W:tA also go a long way toward establishing the feeling of it. There's not a fine progression of powers that you jump through in order to get a talisman or cut a deal; and it doesn't work by being bitten, all the bits are just there right from the beginning. Even Gifts tend to be taught with actions and feelings rather than some kind of lesson in arcane abstractions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:15:19-07:00","id":1106681,"title":"","content":"I've always been a fan of werewolves and superheroes. <br /> <br /> To me, WtA is one of the only splats from the WoD that makes it possible to combine the two with major success. The art, the themes, the antagonists, etc. just scream to me fun.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm eagerly awaiting the Werewolf video game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T14:26:41-07:00","id":1106735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1106484-why-do-people-like-playing-werewolves?p=1106681#post1106681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I'm eagerly awaiting the Werewolf video game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which will lean towards horror element, probably with an early stage 5th edition system.<br /> <br /> Now in topic, I think that the werewolf is the first white wolf game in which you can play a dual life hero. Not only in mood wise but rule wise as well. I mean the first character ever in my first campaign ever was a Nikita-like agent who had a secret agent life and a secret garou life. And in combat was based on his both natures to survive. How can you resist the temptation to play something like that ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T15:01:38-07:00","id":1106749,"title":"","content":"I am a long time fan of Robert E. Howard's work, about people possessing nigh-superhuman physical power and grace (and yes, this is a bit of wish-fullfillment on my part) who manage to stick to a certain degree of personal ethics in a world of corruption and violence. And I tend to agree with his assessment that the human race is more or less doomed to succumb to savagery and barbarism no matter how hard the forces of civilization and progress struggle. But I also feel it's a struggle well worth continuing never the less. So I can relate to the Garou's determination to fight on in spite of the fact that they are almost certainly doomed to lose in the end. I can also empathize with the Garou's issues with Rage and trying to keep it under control, and the depression of Harano. And then I also find the various aspects of survivalism, nature and folk lore interesting, as well as exploring some of the ramifications of an animist cosmology. <br /> <br /> Also, the first horror/monster film I ever saw was Frankenstein Meets the Wolfman (1943), so they've always been my second favorite classic monster (Frankenstein is first), and I grew up watching stuff like An American Werewolf in London, Silver Bullet, Teen Wolf, Monster Squad, Wolfen, and the Werewolf tv series. I'd even managed to dig up back issues of Marvel's Werewolf by Night series when I was still in elementary school, and Wolfsbane is one of my top five all-time X-Men characters. So I've always been a huge werewolf nerd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T22:51:11-07:00","id":1107904,"title":"","content":"Well, aside from all the cool detail of the setting, the game provides, the mythology, the unique viewpoint of the Garou as dual-natured beings and all that, ultimately, what spoke to me from the beginning is the rage against the dying of the world. I know, the &quot;captain planet&quot; angle got laughed at and even neglected sometimes, but in truth, that's the most important part to me. The Garou aren't really werewolves in the usual sense of the world and sometimes I miss a &quot;real&quot; werecreature splat from WoD, just like the ones in nearly every movie, folk tale and urban fantasy novel, but I think WtA is great, because it's central theme is one of the biggest struggles of modern humanity, but not from a human-centric standpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T00:13:28-07:00","id":1108648,"title":"","content":"There is something oh so very appealing on a primal and emotional level about playing passionate warriors raging against injustice and trying to make the world a better place the best they know how to.<br /> <br /> And I bet I'm not the only Dragonball Z fan who finds delightful similarities between the Saiyan Race and the Garou; they are also a Warrior Race of Lycanthropes, albeit Giant Apes in their full-moon induced &quot;Crinos&quot; forms.<br /> <br /> And yes, I REALLY look forward to the day that with a combination of &quot;Lambert Light&quot; and &quot;Silver Body&quot;, I can role play a Silver Fang Warrior modeled after Vegeta (a Warrior Prince) charging singlehandedly into a horde and &quot;Transforming into a Silver Garou Super Saiyan&quot;<br /> <br /> But that's just me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T12:54:59-07:00","id":1108890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1106484-why-do-people-like-playing-werewolves?p=1108648#post1108648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yes, I REALLY look forward to the day that with a combination of &quot;Lambert Light&quot; and &quot;Silver Body&quot;, I can role play a Silver Fang Warrior modeled after Vegeta (a Warrior Prince) charging singlehandedly into a horde and &quot;Transforming into a Silver Garou Super Saiyan&quot;<br /> <br /> But that's just me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean (inhales deeply) Super Saiyan Silver Garou Super Saiyan Silver?<br /> <br /> (The early days before the simplicity of just saying &quot;Super Saiyan Blue&quot;... such grim, and horribly long-winded times...)<br /> <br /> (Also, the typo with &quot;Lambert Light&quot; makes me imagine a Gift where the light cast hits solid objects and projects the Highlander films onto them. (^VVVVVV^) )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T14:14:33-07:00","id":1108930,"title":"","content":"I like it because of the whole Barbarians in modern times angle. The clash of old values and politics with new ones. I once had a DM who complained about Silver Fangs players because to him they always wanted to play the good silver fang and ended up putting bullshit excuses for the tribe. <br /> <br /> To me personally playing the good silver fang, or the good Fenrir or even, god have mercy on you, not-waste-of-space Fianna. Is the whole point of werewolf, not putting BS excuses for the tribes but instead drag them wailing and screaming into a modernity. Even in local games, even if the best the campaign will let you is put only change your Sept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:10:04-07:00","id":1108965,"title":"","content":"I enjoy Werewolf because I think you have the ability to make a compelling character pretty easily (not that other systems don't allow this) as the Garou are highly flawed. They're like recovering alcoholics who have caused so much hurt in the past but are struggling to make amends in the present even though they stumble pretty often. I love the freedom to know definitively what is *wrong* with the world and that it's possible to effect real and bloody change by fighting against corrupt forces or to avenge injustices in the world. Continuing to fight and raise up your head and howl defiance against what is likely a lost cause is a noble sacrifice and one I can respect. Playing Werewolf (if I ever got to play and not GM) scratches all of those itches for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}